## 4. Investment Thesis & Peer Comparison
Core thesis: QCOM’s IP-driven business model generates strong FCF and ROE, despite cyclical risks. While peers like NVIDIA (NVDA) have higher revenue growth, QCOM’s valuation is more attractive on a P/FCF basis.  

**Bull Case:** Strong FCF generation and high ROE will sustain compounding through the cycle.  
**Bear Case:** Apple’s reduced reliance on Qualcomm modems and macroeconomic weakness could depress demand.  

**Verdict:** **BUY** — fundamentals are strong, and FCF is growing despite elevated D/E.  

